    ($SATQ$776cfa7c$SATQ$, $SATQ$bba90b53-4666-4123-babf-8f8dbe2f8a7f$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$6c078e90-6763-4352-b937-ac8fca6ea1ed$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Hana deposited a fixed amount into her bank account each month. The function&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 100 plus 25 t"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>t</mi></math> gives the amount, in dollars, in Hana's bank account after <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> monthly deposits. What is the best interpretation of <math alttext="25"><mn>25</mn>
</math> in this context?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1cc99136-611b-416d-b525-508f618a4e4e","content":"<p>With each monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account increased by <math alttext=\"dollar sign 25\"><mo>$</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"c4e13a46-363c-454e-b825-a4ca8b67fa27","content":"<p>Before Hana made any monthly deposits, the amount in her bank account was&nbsp;<math alttext=\"dollar sign 25\"><mo>$</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"c70859ea-ee5a-4e1d-b46a-4f183b4f833d","content":"<p>After <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account was <math alttext=\"dollar sign 25\"><mo>$</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"1d3ef378-ef5e-48d9-a26a-f00e360e7e88","content":"<p>Hana made a total of <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math> monthly deposits.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1cc99136-611b-416d-b525-508f618a4e4e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. It's given that <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> represents the number of monthly deposits. In the given function&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 100 plus 25 t"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>t</mi></math>, the coefficient of <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="25"><mn>25</mn>
</math>. This means that for every increase in the value of <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, the value of&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis t right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> increases by <math alttext="25"><mn>25</mn>
</math>. It follows that with each monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account increased by <math alttext="dollar sign 25"><mo>$</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect. Before Hana made any monthly deposits, the amount in her bank account was&nbsp;<math alttext="dollar sign 100"><mo>$</mo><mn>100</mn></math>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. After <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account was <math alttext="dollar sign 125"><mo>$</mo><mn>125</mn></math>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"776cfa7c","external_id":"bba90b53-4666-4123-babf-8f8dbe2f8a7f","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"6c078e90-6763-4352-b937-ac8fca6ea1ed","uId":"c7af64c8-342c-40eb-b7f3-038b5fad4353","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.B.","skill_desc":"Linear functions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>Hana deposited a fixed amount into her bank account each month. The function&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 100 plus 25 t\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>t</mi></math> gives the amount, in dollars, in Hana's bank account after <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> monthly deposits. What is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math> in this context?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1cc99136-611b-416d-b525-508f618a4e4e","content":"<p>With each monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account increased by <math alttext=\"dollar sign 25\"><mo>$</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"c4e13a46-363c-454e-b825-a4ca8b67fa27","content":"<p>Before Hana made any monthly deposits, the amount in her bank account was&nbsp;<math alttext=\"dollar sign 25\"><mo>$</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"c70859ea-ee5a-4e1d-b46a-4f183b4f833d","content":"<p>After <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account was <math alttext=\"dollar sign 25\"><mo>$</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p>"},{"id":"1d3ef378-ef5e-48d9-a26a-f00e360e7e88","content":"<p>Hana made a total of <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math> monthly deposits.</p>"}],"keys":["1cc99136-611b-416d-b525-508f618a4e4e"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. It's given that <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> represents the number of monthly deposits. In the given function&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 100 plus 25 t\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>t</mi></math>, the coefficient of <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math>. This means that for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> increases by <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math>. It follows that with each monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account increased by <math alttext=\"dollar sign 25\"><mo>$</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. Before Hana made any monthly deposits, the amount in her bank account was&nbsp;<math alttext=\"dollar sign 100\"><mo>$</mo><mn>100</mn></math>.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. After <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account was <math alttext=\"dollar sign 125\"><mo>$</mo><mn>125</mn></math>.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959811,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"776cfa7c","skill_cd":"H.B.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Linear functions","createDate":1691007959811,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":null,"external_id":"bba90b53-4666-4123-babf-8f8dbe2f8a7f","primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"c7af64c8-342c-40eb-b7f3-038b5fad4353","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["1cc99136-611b-416d-b525-508f618a4e4e"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. It's given that <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> represents the number of monthly deposits. In the given function&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 100 plus 25 t\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>t</mi></math>, the coefficient of <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math>. This means that for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>, the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> increases by <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math>. It follows that with each monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account increased by <math alttext=\"dollar sign 25\"><mo>$</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. Before Hana made any monthly deposits, the amount in her bank account was&nbsp;<math alttext=\"dollar sign 100\"><mo>$</mo><mn>100</mn></math>.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. After <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> monthly deposit, the amount in Hana's bank account was <math alttext=\"dollar sign 125\"><mo>$</mo><mn>125</mn></math>.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p>Hana deposited a fixed amount into her bank account each month. The function&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 100 plus 25 t\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>t</mi></math> gives the amount, in dollars, in Hana's bank account after <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> monthly deposits. What is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math> in this context?</p>","externalid":"bba90b53-4666-4123-babf-8f8dbe2f8a7f","templateid":"52adb7ef-73f3-4808-b303-482202b4e0a6","vaultid":"6c078e90-6763-4352-b937-ac8fca6ea1ed","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"1cc99136-611b-416d-b5